description.narrative:
The overall objective of the project is to improve Ukraine's fulfillment of EU chapter 27 and of Minamata and Stockholm conventions requirements, with a focus on the requirements in the field of waste management.

This will be achieved by supporting the MEPNR in its capacity to manage and prepare the EU-accession process in Chapter 27 of the EU Acquis on environment (with a focus on waste) and by strengthening the capacity of the ministry to implement the legislation through policy- and decision-making and enhancing its communication with waste stakeholders.

The project will have three short term outcome areas:
1. EU accession preparedness of MEPNR strengthened with governance and management arrangements for EU accession in place, (including mandate, planning, financing, policy, legislation);
2. Improved waste management decision and policy making in MEPNR, in line with the Waste Framework directive, the Landfill directive and the Minamata and Stockholm conventions;
3. Improved preparedness of municipalities, regions, and waste entrepreneurs for implementation of Ukraine's national waste management plan.
